Subject: [PATCH 1/8] sc-compose checkpoint 1: composeP_efficient and
 composeV_efficient

New helper modules under SecureComputation/ComposeSecurity/:
- Machines.lean: polynomial-time machines on encoded histories (concatenation over a
  data-dependent range, the iterated second projection, the interleaved-slot map
  polyTimeComputable_slots, strategies as functions of the machine layout, zero padding).
- Efficiency.lean: the shared pieces runW, ansW, mainW and the composed parties composePW,
  composeVW on the layout, their equations with composeP/composeV and polynomial time.
ComposeSecurity.lean: imports both helpers; proofs of composeP_efficient and
composeV_efficient; their sketches describe the delivered proofs; module docstring updated
(polynomial-time paragraph, Contents, Main results). hbcSecure_compose keeps its sorry.
